  "hints": [
    {
      "tr": "Sapmalar örneklemin kendi ortalamasına göre; bu yüzden `n - 1`.",
      "en": "Deviations are from the sample's own mean; that is why `n - 1`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Son satırda `round(total / (n - 1), 3)`.",
      "en": "On the last line, `round(total / (n - 1), 3)`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\ndef sample_var(values):\n    n = len(values)\n    mean = sum(values) / n\n    total = 0\n    for x in values:\n        total += (x - mean) ** 2\n    return round(total / (n - 1), 3)\n\n\nprint(sample_var([2, 4, 4, 5, 7, 9]))\nprint(sample_var([10, 20]))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\ndef sample_var(values):\n    n = len(values)\n    mean = sum(values) / n\n    total = 0\n    for x in values:\n        total += (x - mean) ** 2\n    return round(total / (n - 1), 3)\n\n\nprint(sample_var([2, 4, 4, 5, 7, 9]))\nprint(sample_var([10, 20]))\n```"
    }
  ],
